## Why This Matters More Than It Looks

You spent real effort earlier getting the DB schema right — separate agent rows, separate role grants, per-collection persona filters. That work assumed collection-level granularity would be enforced consistently. This fix quietly downgrades the route-level check to module-level granularity while leaving collection-level enforcement to happen only deeper in the graph.

This is exactly the kind of inconsistency that causes real incidents — not today, but in six months when someone adds a new analytics module and forgets that the graph-level check is secretly the only thing enforcing collection-level RBAC.

