    module_id = AuthController.get_module_id_by_name(module_name, db)
    if module_id is None:
        raise HTTPException(400, f"Unknown module: {module_name}")
    if not AuthController.check_module_access(current_user.emp_no, current_user.group_idx, current_user.role_ids, module_id, db):
        raise HTTPException(403, f"You do not have access to module '{module_name}'.")
```

This preserves exactly what your DB design intended: RMS workflow access and RMS_ANALYTICS access are **independently granted and independently checked**, at the correct layer, the first time, without relying on a second check deeper in the graph to catch what the route guard got wrong.

